WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:06.420
More bio-prank than biopic , "Weird: The Al&nbsp;
Yankovic Story" parodies movie biographies of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:12.585
musicians just like "Weird Al" parodies hit songs.&nbsp;
Fans and critics wouldn't want it any other way.

00:00:12.585 --> 00:00:18.540
The origins of "Weird: The Al Yankovic Story"&nbsp;
date back to 2010, on Funny or Die. The minds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:23.400
behind it put together a trailer for a then-fake&nbsp;
movie of the same name with Aaron Paul from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:28.260
"Breaking Bad" portraying the titular musician.&nbsp;
It garnered some attention online at the time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:32.777
but didn't seem to be anything more than&nbsp;
a one-off sketch. Fast forward 12 years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.777 --> 00:00:35.327
and "The Al Yankovic Story" is a reality.

00:00:35.327 --> 00:00:38.580
"'Bohemian Rhapsody' had come out, and&nbsp;
'Rocketman' was about to come out, so,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:40.378
you know, Al thought it was the right time."

00:00:40.378 --> 00:00:45.840
"Weird" is essentially a parody of music biopics&nbsp;
about a musician who's made a career out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:51.000
song parodies. According to a trailer for the&nbsp;
film, "Weird" will tell the sensationalized and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:56.700
extremely untrue story of the rise and fall of&nbsp;
Yankovic, including how he was discovered in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:01.860
club, devised his first parody on the spot,&nbsp;
allowed himself to be seduced by Madonna,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:08.773
and descended into a haze of drugs, alcohol, and&nbsp;
arrests. Very little of which really happened.

00:01:08.773 --> 00:01:13.860
To pull off an epic tale of fame, love, and&nbsp;
polka, "Weird: The Al Yankovic Story" has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:18.720
assembled quite a cast. First and foremost&nbsp;
is Harry Potter himself, Daniel Radcliffe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:24.060
who The Hollywood Reporter revealed signed&nbsp;
on to play Yankovic in January 2022.

00:01:24.238 --> 00:01:26.578
"How, like, well versed are you on the accordion?"

00:01:27.475 --> 00:01:29.130
"Much better than I was three months ago."

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:34.740
Rainn Wilson of "The Office" joins him as his&nbsp;
mentor, syndicated radio show host Dr. Demento,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:39.060
with Evan Rachel Wood as Madonna,&nbsp;
Quinta Brunson as Oprah Winfrey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:44.100
and Spencer Treat Clark as Yankovic's&nbsp;
longtime bassist, Steve Jay. Toby Huss&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:49.800
and Julianne Nicholson will portray Yankovic's&nbsp;
anti-accordion parents, Nick and Mary Yankovic.

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:53.580
That's just the tip of the iceberg when it&nbsp;
comes to the comedic talent on display in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:57.960
the cast. One name that's missing, though,&nbsp;
is Aaron Paul. The "Westworld" star nearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:01.680
had a spot in the film to honor his role&nbsp;
in the original "Funny or Die" sketch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:05.760
but his cameo never came to pass.&nbsp;
In an interview with CinemaBlend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:10.140
Paul explained that a bout of COVID-19&nbsp;
prevented him from appearing. He said,

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:15.420
"I couldn't do it, and then I was just out for&nbsp;
like 10 solid days. I have never felt more sick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:20.835
in my life. And so we couldn't do the cameo,&nbsp;
which I just absolutely was crushed about."

00:02:20.835 --> 00:02:25.860
Principal photography on "The Al Yankovic&nbsp;
Story" kicked off in February 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:31.140
according to an Instagram post from Yankovic.&nbsp;
By early March, filming had already wrapped,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:35.580
Yankovic later posted on Twitter. After&nbsp;
spending a few months in post-production,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:41.760
"The Al Yankovic Story" will become available for&nbsp;
viewing on November 4, 2022, in the United States.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:47.940
The film made its theatrical debut at the Toronto&nbsp;
International Film Festival in September, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:52.920
there aren't going to be too many other theatrical&nbsp;
showings. "The Al Yankovic Story" will drop as an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:57.900
exclusive on the Roku Channel. The streamer comes&nbsp;
free with the purchase of a Roku stick or box,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:03.736
but folks who don't have either of those can&nbsp;
also access The Roku Channel via a web browser.

00:03:03.736 --> 00:03:07.980
Eric Appel directed "Weird: The Al&nbsp;
Yankovic Story," and it's difficult&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:12.240
to imagine a better choice. After all,&nbsp;
he's the one that spearheaded the original&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:16.740
sketch that got the ball rolling all&nbsp;
those years ago. Appel also boasts an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:20.880
impressive and varied résumé that extends&nbsp;
well beyond the reaches of Funny or Die.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:23.640
In addition to a number of Funny or Die sketches,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:28.800
he's also jumped to television and helmed&nbsp;
episodes of "New Girl," "The Office," "Son&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:34.680
of Zorn," "The Grinder," "Blue Mountain State,"&nbsp;
and "Brooklyn Nine-Nine," among numerous other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:40.560
well-known network and cable programs. Appel has&nbsp;
worked as a writer, producer, and editor as well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:45.420
though he isn't always behind the camera. He's&nbsp;
tried his hand at acting on a small handful of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:50.160
occasions and last appeared on an episode&nbsp;
"Nick Swardson's Pretend Time" in 2010.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:52.440
Appel also wrote the screenplay for "Weird:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:56.450
The Al Yankovic" story, along&nbsp;
with "Weird Al" Yankovic himself.

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:02.280
A teaser for "Weird: The Al Yankovic Story"&nbsp;
arrived in May of 2022. It kicks off with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:06.480
concert venue preparing for what appears&nbsp;
to be a huge act. The crowd is on their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:10.140
feet as they await the musician they're&nbsp;
all there to see, and in mere moments,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:15.600
they get their wish. "Weird Al" Yankovic emerges&nbsp;
on stage — accordion in hand — and prepares to put&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:21.000
on a show. The 1986 track "Like A Surgeon" begins&nbsp;
to play over a string of clips from the film.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:26.040
While not revealing much about the plot, the&nbsp;
montage does provide some interesting tidbits.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:31.140
Yankovic performs at various venues, dazzles&nbsp;
onlookers with his music and dance skills,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:35.640
and even gets into a heated fight at a&nbsp;
restaurant. A stern Yankovic then asks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:39.000
if anyone has an accordion, prompting&nbsp;
three people to hand him an instrument&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:43.920
simultaneously. The teaser closes with the&nbsp;
title card and the lead character confessing,

00:04:44.248 --> 00:04:45.728
"I'm full of surprises."

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:52.560
In August 2022, the full trailer for the movie&nbsp;
hit the internet, revealing more plot beats,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:58.140
moments, and characters. With Daniel Radcliffe&nbsp;
narrating, the preview argues that "Weird" is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:02.640
the origin story of a legendary musician,&nbsp;
showing that he partied harder than anyone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:08.077
You can spy Will Forte and the real "Weird&nbsp;
Al" Yankovic at the end if you look closely.

00:05:08.077 --> 00:05:12.540
Within a few days of the screening of the&nbsp;
"Weird: The Al Yankovic Story" at the Toronto&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:17.880
International Film Festival, movie critics began&nbsp;
to publish their reviews. According to Rotten&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:24.120
Tomatoes, it appears as if "Weird" just might be a&nbsp;
critical darling, earning an exemplary 92% rating.

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:28.920
David Fear of Rolling Stone praised the film&nbsp;
as an extension of the "Weird Al" brand:

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:32.700
"Like the artist himself, 'Weird' knows how&nbsp;
to make fun of something with affection,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:36.000
the [occasional] dollop of&nbsp;
barbed wit and a knack for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:39.180
making imitation seem like the&nbsp;
sincerest form of creativity."

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:42.960
Slant's Mark Hanson wrote that the&nbsp;
film "takes everything to new heights&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:48.240
of glorious ridiculousness." Valerie Complex&nbsp;
of Deadline enjoyed the wide array of cameos,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:51.480
while David Nusair of Reel Film Reviews gushed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:55.380
over Daniel Radcliffe's "completely&nbsp;
captivating, go-for-broke performance."

